#
# The start function is run right after fvwm is done reading
# the config file. This function run after each restart
# so using Test (Init) or Test (Restart) can further control
# actions that are run during the first time run (Init) or
# actions that are run after a restart.
#
DestroyFunc StartFunction
AddToFunc   StartFunction
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec dbus-update-activation-environment --all
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec gnome-keyring-daemon --start --components=secrets
+ I Test (Init, EnvMatch DISPLAY :0) Exec exec xcompmgr -o  -Cc
+ I TestRc (NoMatch) Exec exec hsetroot -center $[infostore.bg]
+ I Test (Init, EnvMatch DISPLAY :0) Exec exec devilspie
+ I Schedule 150 Exec exec hsetroot -center $[infostore.bg]
#+ I Test (Init) Exec exec magick $[infostore.bg] -resize
+ I Module FvwmEvent EventSounds
+ I Module FvwmEvent EventDeIcon
+ I Module FvwmEvent EventChangeFocus
+ I Module FvwmEvent EventRestoreFocus
+ I Module FvwmEvent EventNewDesk
+ I Module FvwmEvent EventIcon
+ I Module FvwmMFL
+ I Module FvwmPager
+ I Module FvwmPerl
#+ I Module FvwmAnimate
###  Shelf.  Not a module, so fvwm won't restart it on its own; kill any
###  running instance and launch a fresh one so a Restart picks up changes
###  to bin/shelf-panel, photon.py, or panel.items, same as everything else
###  StartFunction brings up.  Width/collapse state survives in
###  .panel.state, so the restart is invisible beyond a brief redraw.
+ I Exec exec sh -c 'pkill -f "bin/shelf-panel$"; exec "$FVWM_USERDIR/bin/shelf-panel"'
# Replaced by the shelf panel above, which now carries the window list, tray
# and clock the taskbar used to; lxqt-panel would duplicate all three.
#+ I Test (Init) Exec exec lxqt-panel
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec lxqt-globalkeysd
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec lxqt-notificationd
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec lxqt-policykit-agent
###  fvwm doesn't implement XDG autostart, so spice-vdagent's autostart
###  .desktop entry (/etc/xdg/autostart/spice-vdagent.desktop) never runs on
###  its own. Without it, virt-manager window resizes never reach the guest,
###  so the display stays stuck at the QXL default (1024x768) after every
###  restart. spice-vdagentd (system service) is already running via its
###  socket unit; this just starts the per-session client that talks to it.
###  This config is shared with a bare-metal host, so it's guarded: only
###  fires when the SPICE virtio-serial channel actually exists (i.e. we're
###  really inside a QEMU/SPICE guest) and the binary is installed.
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec sh -c 'test -e /dev/virtio-ports/com.redhat.spice.0 && command -v spice-vdagent >/dev/null && exec spice-vdagent'
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec flameshot
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec easyeffects --gapplication-service
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec nicotine -s
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec xscreensaver
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec kdeconnectd
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec kdeconnect-indicator
#+ I Test (Init) Exec exec sudo firewall-applet
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec nm-applet --indicator
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec gammastep-indicator
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec signal-desktop --use-tray-icon
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec telegram-desktop
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec pactl load-module module-switch-on-connect
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec solaar -w hide 
+ I Test (Init) Exec exec sxhkd
+ I Test (Init) Schedule 1000 Exec exec qlipper
#+ I Test (Init) Schedule 1000 Exec exec ~/.local/opt/activitywatch/start.sh
+ I BugOpts QtDragnDropWorkaround True
###  Prune stale window thumbnails.  Thumbnails expire after 100s and are
###  recaptured on demand, so anything a week old belongs to a window that is
###  long gone.  Without this the cache only grows -- it had reached 9641
###  files / 239MB before the sweep was added.  Runs on restart too; it is a
###  find over a few hundred files.
+ I Exec exec find $[FVWM_USERDIR]/images/thumbs -maxdepth 1 -type f -mtime +7 -delete
+ I Schedule 100 Module Thumbnail
+ I Schedule Periodic 300000 1222 5minutes
+ I Test (EnvMatch DISPLAY :1) Read vnc-overrides

