##   ├ Desktops                                              {{{2
#
# 9 pages on a single Desk (Desk 0). Cells show the Super+<n> binding.
#
#       0   1   2   <- page x
#     +---+---+---+
#   0 | 1 | 2 | 3 |
#     +---+---+---+
#   1 | 4 | 5 | 6 |
#     +---+---+---+
#   2 | 7 | 8 | 9 |
#     +---+---+---+
#   ^ page y
#
EwmhNumberOfDesktops 1 0
DesktopSize 3x3
EdgeScroll 100 100
EdgeResistance -1
EdgeThickness 1
Style * EdgeMoveDelay 250
Style * EdgeMoveResistance 20
Style * EdgeResizeDelay -1

# EwmhBaseStruts [left] [right] [top] [bottom]
# Reserves space along the edge(s) of the Screen that will not
# be covered when maximizing or placing windows.
# The shelf claims the right column; there is no bottom row any more.
##  The shelf is resizable, so its width is whatever the panel last saved
##  rather than a constant.  The panel re-issues this itself as you drag the
##  edge -- EwmhBaseStruts does take effect at runtime -- and this line is
##  what gets it right again after a Restart, which re-reads the config.  The
##  panel itself is restarted along with fvwm (see the StartFunction line
##  above that pkills and relaunches it), so this is only for the moment
##  between the config re-read and the panel coming back up.
PipeRead "echo EwmhBaseStruts 0 \
    $($[FVWM_USERDIR]/bin/shelf-panel --print-width) 0 0"

